infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What belongs in middleware — and what must live deeper
  desc Cheap, request-shaped decisions run before routing; storage-touching work is a per-request tax
  compares
    - label Belongs in middleware — cheap, request-shaped, pre-routing
      children
        - label Locale + A/B + legacy redirects
          desc Read Accept-Language/geo, bucket via cookie, rewrite — URL stays
        - label Optimistic auth UX
          desc No session cookie? bounce to /login before the page renders
        - label Cookie presence / web-crypto verify
          desc Reads what is in the request — no storage round-trip
        - label Request ID + bot filtering
          desc Set a header; microsecond cost across every request
    - label Belongs deeper — route handler / data layer
      children
        - label Session lookup against the DB
          desc 35ms tax on every matched request — and every Link prefetch
        - label Per-resource authorization
          desc The enforcing check — the tier that survives the CVE bypass
        - label ORM / TCP drivers / native modules
          desc Do not load on the classic Edge runtime (Node middleware: 15.5+)
        - label Heavy JWT libraries
          desc Cryptic bundling errors when imported into middleware.ts
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
